2:T445,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice#blogposting","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice","headline":"5 tips to improve your radio voice","url":"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Guy Harris","url":"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/voiceoverguy","image":"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/assets/images/guy-harris-profile.jpg"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"VoiceoverGuy","url":"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/assets/images/guy-harris-voiceover.png"}},"inLanguage":"en-GB","isAccessibleForFree":true,"description":"Discover 5 key tips from Guy Harris to improve your radio voice, boost confidence, sharpen delivery, and sound more polished whether live or pre-recorded.","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/assets/img/blog/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice4.jpg"}}6:["slug","five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice","d"]
0:["XPBGwEKvr8cwSZUTNZgMN",[[["",{"children":[["slug","five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"slug\":\"five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice\"}",{}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":[["slug","five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",[[["$","script","schema-0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","script","schema-1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"News & Blog\",\"item\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/voiceover-news\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"5 tips to improve your radio voice\",\"item\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice\"}]}"}}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"5 tips to improve your radio voice"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header-sub","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<p>If you are considering a career in voiceover or in radio broadcasting, then you probably already\r\nsuspect that your voice sounds nicer than the average person’s. Perhaps you’ve been complemented\r\non your voice before or perhaps you’ve even done a little amateur radio broadcasting while at\r\nuniversity… Whichever angle you’re coming from, it never hurts to work on your skills, so here are\r\nfive tips to improve your radio voice.</p>"}}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-post-body","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-main one-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>1) Be Yourself</h2>\r\n<p>When many people enter into a voiceover or radio broadcasting career, they try to imitate their\r\nfavourite radio celebrities, or they perhaps try to sound a little like actors or musicians famous for\r\ntheir voices. However, the more effort you put into trying to sound like James Earl Jones, the less\r\ntime you’ll have to develop your own sound. And, in the world of radio voiceover, your sound is your\r\nidentity. Being yourself also has an added bonus, as radio broadcasting has become increasingly\r\ninformal, meaning that a more relaxed tone and demeanour is actually exactly what a modern\r\naudience expects.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n"}}],false,false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice4.jpg","alt":"Radio Voiceover: Five tips to improve your radio voice","className":"blog-post-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>2) Record Your Voice in Professional and Casual Settings</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>No matter how much of a natural you are, you’ll still need to practice, and for a voiceover artist or\r\nradio presenter this involves listening to recordings of your voice, both when you’re on the radio and\r\njust when you’re having a conversation with your friends in the pub. Compare your tone of voice, its\r\ndepth, clarity, warmth, etc, and compare how natural you sound in both settings. If you can isolate\r\nhow you sound when you’re just chatting with friends, you can bring that natural demeanour to your\r\nradio shows, this is especially valuable if you have to often read from scripts as doing so can make\r\nyour voice sound flat and unexciting.</p>"}}]]}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>3) Consider Your Accent Very Carefully</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Gone are the days of the stilted BBC RP accent where most broadcasters sounded the same. Radio\r\npresenters all over the UK now come from… all over the UK. Regional accents are absolutely fine for\r\nradio, but you may have to standardise parts of your accent or at least lose some of the more\r\nesoteric dialect words. Listen to other regional radio presenters to figure out how to strike balance\r\nbetween regional and standard English. If you can find this balance you can work in both local and\r\ncountry-wide radio broadcasting. You don’t have to lose your voice’s regional identity, but you can\r\nprobably temper it slightly, making it more appealing (and understandable) to a wider audience.</p>"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice2.jpg","alt":"Radio Voiceover: Five tips to improve your radio voice","className":"blog-post-img"}]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice3.jpg","alt":"Radio Voiceover: Five tips to improve your radio voice","className":"blog-post-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>4) Practise Your Improvisational Skills</h2>\r\n<p>Working in radio often requires you to think on your feet, especially when talking to the public\r\nover the phone. Phone-ins are necessarily off script, as are most interviews. Sure, you can write out\r\nthe questions, but you can’t predict all of the answers ahead of time. It’s also important that you\r\ndevelop your ad-libbing skills as you will probably often find yourself reading out badly written\r\nscripts. If you can quickly ad-lib a script to suit your own voice and style, you’ll sound much more\r\nnatural to your audience. It’s difficult to fast-track your improvisation and ad-lib skills, as they’re\r\nskills you develop on the job, but if you keep these skills in your mind, you’ll be able jump on the\r\nright opportunities and be ready for potential pitfalls.</p>"}}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>5) Edit Your Radio Scripts</h2>\r\n<p>Many people who start working in radio are surprised that most presenters, no matter how\r\nnatural they sound, work from scripts. Scripts keep even the most seasoned professionals from\r\nmeandering into conversational cul-de- sacs. However, even a well-written script may not suit your\r\nparticular style, dialect, or voice. Improv and ad-libbing will only get you so far, so a little scan over\r\nthe script before the show is always a good way to iron out any kinks and make sure your show runs\r\nsmoothly. Take a red pen and make a few notes for yourself and don’t be afraid to rewrite\r\nsomething in your own voice. As long as the message is similar, there shouldn’t be a problem.</p>"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice4.jpg","alt":"Radio Voiceover: Five tips to improve your radio voice","className":"blog-post-img"}]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-bottom-text","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<p>That’s it for this radio voiceover guide. I hope readers have learned a few practical tips to improve\r\ntheir radio voiceover skills. If you’re interested in Guy’s voiceover skills, check out his <a href=\"/commercial-voiceover\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"commercial\r\nvoiceover reel\">commercial\r\nvoiceover reel</a> or get in touch and request a bespoke sample of your script.</p>"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-cta","children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/voiceover-news","className":"cta-btn cta-btn--outline","children":"← Back to News & Blog"}]}],["$","$L4",null,{"pageTitle":"5 tips to improve your radio voice","pageUrl":"five-tips-to-improve-your-radio-voice"}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-related-strip","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-grid","children":[["$","$L3","740",{"href":"/doggie-doo-voice-over","className":"blog-related-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-img-wrap","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/doggie-doo-voice-over.jpg","alt":"doggie-doo-voice-over","className":"blog-related-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-title","children":"Doggie Doo voice over"}]]}],["$","$L3","925",{"href":"/big-super-hero-voiceover","className":"blog-related-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-img-wrap","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/big-super-hero-voiceover.jpg","alt":"big-super-hero-voiceover","className":"blog-related-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-title","children":"Big American Super Hero Voice"}]]}],["$","$L3","568",{"href":"/virgin-holidays-voice","className":"blog-related-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-img-wrap","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/virgin-holidays-voice.jpg","alt":"Virgin Holidays Voice","className":"blog-related-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-title","children":"Virgin Holidays Voice"}]]}]]}]}]}]],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L5",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","$6","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L7",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[[["$","link","0",{"rel":"stylesheet","href":"/_next/static/css/913cecfa117908b5.css","precedence":"n